WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.150
Around the newborn Sun swirls a disk of leftovers:

2
00:00:04.097 --> 00:00:07.413
gas, ice, and dust forged in dead stars.

3
00:00:09.072 --> 00:00:10.598
Dust sticks to dust.

4
00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:12.943
Pebbles become boulders.

5
00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:16.509
Boulders become mountains, miles wide.

6
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.917
Then gravity takes over.

7
00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:24.393
The bigger they get, the harder they pull, and the faster they grow.

8
00:00:26.064 --> 00:00:28.472
Near the Sun, ice can't survive.

9
00:00:29.132 --> 00:00:31.882
So the inner planets are built from rock and metal.

10
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.764
One world outgrows its neighbors.

11
00:00:36.424 --> 00:00:38.911
Every crash makes it bigger, and hotter.

12
00:00:40.584 --> 00:00:42.031
Hot enough to melt.

13
00:00:42.692 --> 00:00:45.297
Iron sinks to the center and becomes a core.

14
00:00:45.955 --> 00:00:48.034
Lighter rock rises to the top.

15
00:00:49.692 --> 00:00:50.955
No oceans.

16
00:00:51.616 --> 00:00:53.063
No breathable air.

17
00:00:53.721 --> 00:00:55.247
No solid ground.

18
00:00:55.905 --> 00:00:59.681
Just a glowing ocean of magma under a sky of ash and steam.

19
00:01:01.344 --> 00:01:05.965
This is Earth, 4.54 billion years ago.

20
00:01:05.728 --> 00:01:07.623
And its worst day is still coming.

